IMPORT prelude

-- Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- Edition: Act No. 111/1986, Version No. 159, incorporating amendments as at 1 November 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/transport-accident-act-1986.txt, a plain-text conversion of the Word file the owner
-- saved by hand on 2026-11-06; the equations lost in conversion are in transport-accident-act-1986.formulas.md beside
-- it. Line numbers below are lines of that text.
--
-- FIGURES. The Act prints its dollar amounts as they were last written into it, and s 61 (lines 2083-2142) varies
-- them every 1 July by average weekly earnings or the Melbourne consumer price index. No instrument stating the
-- varied amounts is deposited (none was found in the Gazette, see subjects/au/vic/README.md), so every function that
-- needs a varied amount takes it as an input; the Act's printed figures are named below for the cases and as a gloss.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- A period "after" a day does not count that day (the reading of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic)
-- s 44, which is not deposited). So "within 28 days of receiving" a notice ends 28 days later; "within one year after
-- the accident" ends on the same date a year later. READING, recorded in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `a` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` `is on or before` `b` THEN `b` ELSE `a`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `a` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` `is on or before` `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same date n months later (n may be negative); where that month is shorter, its last day.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY
        (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`))
        `the new month`
        `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS `months after` (`n` TIMES 12) `the day`

-- The day a person born on a day attains an age (a person born on 29 February attains it on 28 February in a
-- year that is not a leap year: READING).
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER, `the day of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of attaining age` `the age` `the day of birth` MEANS `years after` `the age` `the day of birth`

-- The day of the accident, or the day the injury first manifested itself, whichever is later (s 4(1A), s 43(1),
-- s 46A(1AB)); s 3(4) (line 298) reads "18 months after the accident" as 18 months after the injury first manifests.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the day the injury first manifested itself` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the time counts from` `the day of the accident` `the day the injury first manifested itself` MEANS
    `the later of` `the day of the accident` `the day the injury first manifested itself`

§§ `The Act's printed figures (s 61 varies each every 1 July)`

-- The weekly payment figures of ss 44, 45 and 58 (lines 1092-1105, 1115-1146, 1727-1741) and of ss 49 and 50
-- (lines 1450-1464, 1495-1510), as printed. s 61(1) varies them by average weekly earnings.
DECLARE `Weekly payment figures` HAS
    `the base amount`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the amount for one dependant`          IS A NUMBER
    `the amount for each other dependant`   IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum`                           IS A NUMBER

`the printed figures of ss 44, 45 and 58` MEANS
    `Weekly payment figures` WITH
        `the base amount`                     IS 304
        `the amount for one dependant`        IS 85
        `the amount for each other dependant` IS 27
        `the maximum`                         IS 621

`the printed figures of ss 49 and 50` MEANS
    `Weekly payment figures` WITH
        `the base amount`                     IS 270
        `the amount for one dependant`        IS 76
        `the amount for each other dependant` IS 25
        `the maximum`                         IS 504

-- Other printed figures, with the line and the index that varies each.
`the printed s 53(3)(b) limit` MEANS 99220                     -- line 1583; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 54A(5)(a) maximum` MEANS 965                    -- line 1623; AWE, s 61(2C)
`the printed s 57 and s 59(4) amount` MEANS 103210             -- lines 1690, 1802; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 59(3)(a) weekly amount` MEANS 59                -- line 1793; AWE, s 61(1)
`the printed s 59(6)(a) education allowance` MEANS 1660        -- line 1812; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 60(2A)(b) funeral limit` MEANS 14135            -- line 1913; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 60(2CA) limit` MEANS 10000                      -- line 1933; AWE, s 61(1) (not in the s 61(2) list)
`the printed s 60A(4) limit` MEANS 3500                        -- line 2068; AWE, s 61(1) (not in the s 61(2) list)
`the printed s 93(7) threshold` MEANS 30520                    -- lines 2613-2616; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 93(7)(a) maximum` MEANS 686840                  -- line 2614; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 93(7)(b) maximum` MEANS 305250                  -- line 2617; CPI, s 61(2)
`the printed s 93(9) maximum` MEANS 500000                     -- line 2619; CPI, s 61(2)

-- The dependants' figure of ss 44(2)(c), 45(2)(c), 45(4)(c), 49(2)(c), 50(2)(c), 58(2)(c): the base amount, plus the
-- amount for one dependant, plus the amount for each other dependant; the base alone with no dependants ((b)).
GIVEN `the figures` IS A `Weekly payment figures`, `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants` MEANS
    IF `the number of dependants` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the figures`'s `the base amount`
    ELSE     `the figures`'s `the base amount`
        PLUS `the figures`'s `the amount for one dependant`
        PLUS ((`the number of dependants` MINUS 1) TIMES `the figures`'s `the amount for each other dependant`)

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- entitlement to compensation (ss 35-42)`

DECLARE `Where the accident occurred` IS ONE OF
    `in Victoria`
    `in another State or in a Territory`
    `outside Australia`

DECLARE `What the accident involved` IS ONE OF
    `a motor vehicle or a pedal cycle, other than a recreation vehicle`
    `a recreation vehicle only`
    `a railway train or a tram`

-- s 41(1) (lines 988-994): the people a race or speed trial exclusion reaches.
DECLARE `Part in an organised race or speed trial` IS ONE OF
    `no part in one`
    `a driver, passenger or rider in a vehicle or cycle taking part`
    `a spectator, official, organiser or helper`
    `a cyclist taking part, hit by a vehicle not taking part`

-- s 35(1) (lines 800-807): "A person who is injured as a result of a transport accident is entitled to compensation in
-- accordance with this Act if (a) the accident occurred in Victoria; or (b) ... in another State or in a Territory and
-- involved a registered motor vehicle and ... the person was (i) a resident of Victoria; or (ii) the driver of, or a
-- passenger in, the registered motor vehicle." An "if" list: outside it, JUST FALSE (the rule of 2026-10-29).
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where the accident occurred`
      `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a resident of Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(1) -- the person is entitled to compensation` `where` `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `the person was a resident of Victoria` `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `where`
    WHEN `in Victoria` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in another State or in a Territory` THEN
            `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle`
        AND (   `the person was a resident of Victoria`
             OR `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle`)
    WHEN `outside Australia` THEN FALSE

-- s 36 (lines 812-817): where the only reasons are (a) not resident and (b) not the driver or a passenger, in an
-- interstate accident with a registered motor vehicle, "the Commission may pay compensation ... if the Commission is
-- satisfied that that person was, on that date, likely to reside in Victoria for not less than six months". The
-- Commission's satisfaction is an input (a judgment left to it).
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where the accident occurred`
      `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a resident of Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36 -- the Commission may pay compensation` `where` `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `the person was a resident of Victoria` `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months` IF
        `where` EQUALS `in another State or in a Territory`
    AND `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle`
    AND (NOT `the person was a resident of Victoria`)
    AND (NOT `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle`)
    AND `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months`

-- s 39(1), (2) (lines 872-884): not liable if, for a motor vehicle or pedal cycle (other than a recreation vehicle),
-- no report is made to a police officer (in Victoria) or to the police of the other State or Territory, or, for a
-- railway train or a tram, no report is made to its operator; (2) unless, for a motor vehicle, "the Commission
-- determines that in all the circumstances the failure should be excused". A recreation vehicle alone needs no report.
-- READING: "motor vehicle or pedal cycle" read as the accident involving either; the (2) excuse is given to an
-- accident "involving a motor vehicle", read as any accident in the first kind.
GIVEN `the accident involved` IS A `What the accident involved`
      `a report was made to the police or the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission excused the failure to report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1) -- the Commission is not liable because no report was made` `the accident involved` `a report was made to the police or the operator` `the Commission excused the failure to report` IF
    CONSIDER `the accident involved`
    WHEN `a motor vehicle or a pedal cycle, other than a recreation vehicle` THEN
            (NOT `a report was made to the police or the operator`)
        AND (NOT `the Commission excused the failure to report`)
    WHEN `a railway train or a tram` THEN NOT `a report was made to the police or the operator`
    WHEN `a recreation vehicle only` THEN FALSE

-- s 41(1), (1A), (1B) (lines 986-1005): not liable for a driver, passenger or rider in a vehicle or cycle taking part
-- in an organised race or speed trial, or a spectator, official, organiser or helper; unless the race is run under the
-- Road Safety Act and the Commission has certified (1A); but liable to a cyclist taking part who is hit by a vehicle
-- not taking part (1B).
GIVEN `the part` IS A `Part in an organised race or speed trial`
      `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 -- the Commission is not liable because of a race or speed trial` `the part` `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission` IF
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `no part in one` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a cyclist taking part, hit by a vehicle not taking part` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission`

-- ss 37, 38A (lines 819-833, 868-869): not liable to a person who is, or appears to the Commission to be, entitled to
-- compensation for the injury under the Accident Compensation Act 1985, the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and
-- Compensation Act 2013, or a scheme listed in s 37(1). s 41A (lines 1010-1019): an unregistered motor vehicle on
-- private land. s 41B (lines 1022-1030): the owner of an uninsured motor vehicle on private land. s 42(2) (lines
-- 1038-1051): compensation or damages paid, awarded, settled, accepted or sued for under the law of a place outside
-- Victoria, unless the Commission is liable under s 94(1). Each is a flat "not liable": JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where the accident occurred`
      `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a resident of Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to workers' compensation or another s 37 scheme for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accident involved` IS A `What the accident involved`
      `a report was made to the police or the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission excused the failure to report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part` IS A `Part in an organised race or speed trial`
      `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accident involved an unregistered motor vehicle on private land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owned an uninsured motor vehicle driven on private land in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has recovered, settled or sued under the law of another place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is liable under s 94(1) under that law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 35-42 -- the Commission is liable, or may pay, compensation for the injury` `where` `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `the person was a resident of Victoria` `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months` `the person is entitled to workers' compensation or another s 37 scheme for the injury` `the accident involved` `a report was made to the police or the operator` `the Commission excused the failure to report` `the part` `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission` `the accident involved an unregistered motor vehicle on private land` `the person owned an uninsured motor vehicle driven on private land in the accident` `the person has recovered, settled or sued under the law of another place` `the Commission is liable under s 94(1) under that law` IF
        (   `s 35(1) -- the person is entitled to compensation` `where` `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `the person was a resident of Victoria` `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle`
         OR `s 36 -- the Commission may pay compensation` `where` `the accident involved a registered motor vehicle` `the person was a resident of Victoria` `the person was the driver of or a passenger in the registered motor vehicle` `the Commission is satisfied the person was likely to reside in Victoria for at least six months`)
    AND (NOT `the person is entitled to workers' compensation or another s 37 scheme for the injury`)
    AND (NOT (`s 39(1) -- the Commission is not liable because no report was made` `the accident involved` `a report was made to the police or the operator` `the Commission excused the failure to report`))
    AND (NOT (`s 41 -- the Commission is not liable because of a race or speed trial` `the part` `the race is run under the Road Safety Act and certified by the Commission`))
    AND (NOT `the accident involved an unregistered motor vehicle on private land`)
    AND (NOT `the person owned an uninsured motor vehicle driven on private land in the accident`)
    AND (NOT (`the person has recovered, settled or sued under the law of another place` AND (NOT `the Commission is liable under s 94(1) under that law`)))

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- what a conviction does (ss 39(3), 40)`

-- The convictions ss 39(3) and 40 name, in respect of driving a motor vehicle at the time of the accident (except
-- the first head of s 39(3)(a)). "Corresponding laws" of other places are read in with each head.
DECLARE `Conviction` IS ONE OF
    `no conviction`
    `murder, manslaughter or Crimes Act s 5A, involving a motor vehicle`        -- s 39(3)(a)
    `Crimes Act s 318(1) or 319(1)`                                            -- s 39(3)(b): culpable or dangerous driving causing death or serious injury
    `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(a)`                                               -- under the influence: s 40(1)(a), (3)(a)
    `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(b), (f) or (g)`                                   -- prescribed concentration of alcohol: s 40(3)(b), (4), (5)
    `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bb), (h) or (i)`                                  -- drugs: s 40(4A), (5A)
    `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bc) or (j)`                                       -- alcohol and drugs: s 40(3A), (3B), (4B), (5B)
    `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(ba), (c), (ca), (d), (e), (ea) or (eb), 56(2) or 56(7)` -- refusals and failures: s 40(2)

-- s 40(1)(c), (6) (lines 902-905, 950-954): the licence of a driver of a motor vehicle.
DECLARE `Licence at the time` IS ONE OF
    `held a licence for that class of vehicle`
    `had never held a licence for that class (not counting a supervised learner)`
    `licence suspended or cancelled`
    `licence not renewed for at least 3 years`

DECLARE `What a conviction does` HAS
    `the share of loss of earnings compensation payable (ss 44, 45)`              IS A NUMBER
    `impairment and earning capacity benefits are payable (ss 47, 49, 50, 51)`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `compensation other than under s 60 is payable`                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- Each head, with its "unless the person satisfies the Commission that [it] did not contribute in any way to the
-- transport accident" taken as an input (a judgment left to the Commission).
-- s 40(5) (lines 938-942), as converted, prints "0·05", "0·12", "0·24"; s 40(3)(b), (3A)(b), (4)(b) print "024" and
-- "005", read as 0·24 and 0·05 (finding 2). s 40(3)(b): 0·24 or more; s 40(4)(b): more than 0·05; s 40(5): reduced
-- by one-third if more than 0·05 and less than 0·12, by two-thirds if 0·12 or more and less than 0·24, not payable if
-- 0·24 or more. s 40(5B): one-third in any case, and a further one-third if 0·12 or more and less than 0·24.
GIVEN `the person was driving a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction` IS A `Conviction`
      `the concentration of alcohol` IS A NUMBER
      `the person satisfies the Commission it did not contribute to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owned the vehicle and its transport accident charge was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence` IS A `Licence at the time`
      `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence and the person is convicted of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a conviction does`
`ss 39(3), 40 -- what a conviction or the circumstances do` `the person was driving a motor vehicle at the time` `the conviction` `the concentration of alcohol` `the person satisfies the Commission it did not contribute to the accident` `the person owned the vehicle and its transport accident charge was unpaid` `the licence` `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence and the person is convicted of it` MEANS
    `What a conviction does` WITH
        `the share of loss of earnings compensation payable (ss 44, 45)` IS
            IF `nothing but s 60` OR `no loss of earnings at all`
            THEN 0
            ELSE 1 MINUS `the s 40(5), (5A), (5B) reduction`
        `impairment and earning capacity benefits are payable (ss 47, 49, 50, 51)` IS
            NOT (`nothing but s 60` OR `no impairment or earning capacity benefits`)
        `compensation other than under s 60 is payable` IS NOT `nothing but s 60`
    WHERE
        `driving` MEANS `the person was driving a motor vehicle at the time`
        `excused` MEANS `the person satisfies the Commission it did not contribute to the accident`
        `c` MEANS `the concentration of alcohol`
        -- s 39(3)(a) needs no driving; s 39(3)(b) does.
        `nothing but s 60` MEANS
                `the conviction` EQUALS `murder, manslaughter or Crimes Act s 5A, involving a motor vehicle`
            OR  (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Crimes Act s 318(1) or 319(1)`)
        -- s 40(1)(a)-(d) and s 40(2): no compensation under s 44 or 45.
        `no loss of earnings at all` MEANS
                (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(a)` AND (NOT `excused`))
            OR  `the person owned the vehicle and its transport accident charge was unpaid`
            OR  (`driving` AND (NOT (`the licence` EQUALS `held a licence for that class of vehicle`)))
            OR  `the vehicle was used in an indictable offence and the person is convicted of it`
            OR  (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(ba), (c), (ca), (d), (e), (ea) or (eb), 56(2) or 56(7)`)
        -- s 40(2), (3), (3A)-(3B): no compensation under s 47, 49, 50 or 51.
        `no impairment or earning capacity benefits` MEANS
                (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(ba), (c), (ca), (d), (e), (ea) or (eb), 56(2) or 56(7)`)
            OR  (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(a)` AND (NOT `excused`))
            OR  (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(b), (f) or (g)` AND `c` AT LEAST 0.24 AND (NOT `excused`))
            OR  (`driving` AND `the conviction` EQUALS `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bc) or (j)` AND `c` AT LEAST 0.24 AND (NOT `excused`))
        `the s 40(5), (5A), (5B) reduction` MEANS
            IF (NOT `driving`) OR `excused`
            THEN 0
            ELSE CONSIDER `the conviction`
                 WHEN `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(b), (f) or (g)` THEN
                     IF `c` AT LEAST 0.24 THEN 1
                     ELSE IF `c` AT LEAST 0.12 THEN 2 DIVIDED BY 3
                          ELSE IF `c` GREATER THAN 0.05 THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 3
                               ELSE 0
                 WHEN `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bb), (h) or (i)` THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 3
                 WHEN `Road Safety Act s 49(1)(bc) or (j)` THEN
                     IF `c` AT LEAST 0.12 AND `c` LESS THAN 0.24
                     THEN 2 DIVIDED BY 3
                     ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3
                 OTHERWISE 0

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- loss of earnings in the first 18 months (ss 43, 44, 45, 46(2))`

-- The last day of "the first 18 months after the accident" (ss 44(4)(b), 45(6)(b)), counted from the relevant day
-- (s 3(4)); extended by s 46(2) (line 1205) to the day a review not completed within those 18 months is completed.
GIVEN `the relevant day` IS A DATE
      `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the review was completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 44(4)(b), 45(6)(b), 46(2) -- the last day of the period of entitlement` `the relevant day` `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months` `the day the review was completed` MEANS
    IF `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months`
    THEN `the later of` (`months after` 18 `the relevant day`) `the day the review was completed`
    ELSE `months after` 18 `the relevant day`

-- s 43(1), (2) and s 44(4)(a) (lines 1069-1079, 1106-1108): no compensation for loss of earnings during "the first
-- five days ... in respect of which, or any part of which, the earner suffers any loss of earnings", unless the
-- Commission "is satisfied that the earner would suffer acute financial hardship". READING: the first five days on
-- which earnings are lost, counted from the relevant day. "does not include": JUST FALSE outside the period.
GIVEN `the relevant day` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the number of earlier days with lost earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the review was completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 43, 44(4), 45(6) -- the day is in the period of entitlement` `the relevant day` `the day` `the number of earlier days with lost earnings` `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship` `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months` `the day the review was completed` IF
        `the relevant day` `is on or before` `the day`
    AND `the day` `is on or before` (`ss 44(4)(b), 45(6)(b), 46(2) -- the last day of the period of entitlement` `the relevant day` `a review under s 46(1) was not completed within the 18 months` `the day the review was completed`)
    AND (   `the number of earlier days with lost earnings` AT LEAST 5
         OR `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship`)

DECLARE `Earlier accident payment` IS ONE OF
    `no payment for an earlier transport accident`
    `a s 44 weekly payment for an earlier transport accident`
    `a s 45 weekly payment for an earlier transport accident`

-- s 44(2), (3) (lines 1085-1105): the greatest of (a) 80% of pre-accident weekly earnings, (ab) 100% of a s 44 weekly
-- payment for a previous transport accident, (ac) 80% of the pre-accident weekly earnings before a previous accident
-- if a s 45 payment is being received for it, and (b)/(c) the dependants' amount; not more than the lesser of the
-- s 44(3)(a) maximum and 100% of pre-accident weekly earnings.
GIVEN `the figures` IS A `Weekly payment figures`
      `pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `the earlier payment` IS AN `Earlier accident payment`
      `the earlier s 44 weekly payment` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44 -- the weekly payment for total loss of earnings` `the figures` `pre-accident weekly earnings` `the number of dependants` `the earlier payment` `the earlier s 44 weekly payment` `pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident` MEANS
    min `the uncapped amount` (min (`the figures`'s `the maximum`) `pre-accident weekly earnings`)
    WHERE
        `the (ab) amount` MEANS
            IF `the earlier payment` EQUALS `a s 44 weekly payment for an earlier transport accident`
            THEN `the earlier s 44 weekly payment`
            ELSE 0
        `the (ac) amount` MEANS
            IF `the earlier payment` EQUALS `a s 45 weekly payment for an earlier transport accident`
            THEN 0.8 TIMES `pre-accident weekly earnings before the earlier accident`
            ELSE 0
        `the uncapped amount` MEANS
            maximum (LIST (0.8 TIMES `pre-accident weekly earnings`), `the (ab) amount`, `the (ac) amount`, (`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants`))

-- s 45(2)-(5) (lines 1110-1146). Employed: the greater of (a) 85% of the difference between current weekly earnings
-- and pre-accident weekly earnings and (b)/(c) the dependants' amount less actual weekly earnings; not more than the
-- lesser of the maximum less current weekly earnings and 100% of pre-accident weekly earnings less actual weekly
-- earnings. Not employed: as s 44(2)(a)-(c), (3). The Act says "current weekly earnings" in (2)(a) and (3)(a) and
-- "actual weekly earnings" in (2)(b), (c) and (3)(b); one figure is used for both (finding 4). READING: never less
-- than nil. s 45(5A): the pre-accident weekly earnings are those before a previous accident, as the input states.
GIVEN `the figures` IS A `Weekly payment figures`
      `pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `the earner is employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earner's weekly earnings in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 -- the weekly payment for partial loss of earnings` `the figures` `pre-accident weekly earnings` `the number of dependants` `the earner is employed` `the earner's weekly earnings in the week` MEANS
    IF `the earner is employed`
    THEN max 0 (min `the employed amount` `the employed cap`)
    ELSE min (max (0.8 TIMES `pre-accident weekly earnings`) (`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants`))
             (min (`the figures`'s `the maximum`) `pre-accident weekly earnings`)
    WHERE
        `e` MEANS `the earner's weekly earnings in the week`
        `the employed amount` MEANS
            max (0.85 TIMES (`pre-accident weekly earnings` MINUS `e`))
                ((`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants`) MINUS `e`)
        `the employed cap` MEANS
            min ((`the figures`'s `the maximum`) MINUS `e`) (`pre-accident weekly earnings` MINUS `e`)

-- s 45AA(2) (lines 1157-1162): a self-employed earner with a total loss of earnings is paid "75% of the amount
-- specified for the purposes of section 44(3)(a)" until the first of: the period of entitlement ends, the first 12
-- weeks of it end, or the Commission determines pre-accident weekly earnings.
GIVEN `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45AA -- the interim weekly payment to a self-employed earner` `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` MEANS
    0.75 TIMES `the s 44(3)(a) maximum`

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- loss of earning capacity after 18 months (ss 49-53)`

DECLARE `Loss of earning capacity` IS ONE OF
    `total loss of earning capacity`
    `partial loss of earning capacity`

-- s 49(2), (3) (lines 1446-1465): total loss; s 50(2), (3) and s 52 (lines 1491-1511, 1557-1558): partial loss, nothing
-- if "the difference between the earner's pre-accident earning capacity and post-accident earning capacity ... is less
-- than 10 per centum of the pre-accident earning capacity". Both capacities are amounts the Commission determines
-- (ss 49(5), 49(5A), 50(5)), taken as inputs. READING: never less than nil.
GIVEN `the figures` IS A `Weekly payment figures`
      `the loss` IS A `Loss of earning capacity`
      `pre-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER
      `post-accident earning capacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 49, 50, 52 -- the weekly payment for loss of earning capacity` `the figures` `the loss` `pre-accident earning capacity` `post-accident earning capacity` `the number of dependants` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the loss`
    WHEN `total loss of earning capacity` THEN
        min (max (0.8 TIMES `pre-accident earning capacity`) (`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants`))
            (min (`the figures`'s `the maximum`) `pre-accident earning capacity`)
    WHEN `partial loss of earning capacity` THEN
        IF (`pre-accident earning capacity` MINUS `post-accident earning capacity`) LESS THAN (0.1 TIMES `pre-accident earning capacity`)
        THEN 0
        ELSE max 0 (min `the partial amount` `the partial cap`)
    WHERE
        `the partial amount` MEANS
            max (0.85 TIMES (`pre-accident earning capacity` MINUS `post-accident earning capacity`))
                ((`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependants`) MINUS `post-accident earning capacity`)
        `the partial cap` MEANS
            min ((`the figures`'s `the maximum`) MINUS `post-accident earning capacity`)
                (`pre-accident earning capacity` MINUS `post-accident earning capacity`)

-- s 51(2) (lines 1545-1551; formula 86-111a159-F1, A x B / (C - D)): a person other than an earner or a minor gets the
-- s 49 or s 50 amount "less an amount calculated in accordance with the formula", where B is "the number of years
-- before the person attains pension age during which the person is reasonably likely not to be employed" (a judgment,
-- an input), C the pension age and D the age in whole years. NOTHING at or over pension age (C - D not positive: the
-- formula cannot be worked).
GIVEN `the s 49 or s 50 amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the years likely not to be employed before pension age` IS A NUMBER
      `the pension age` IS A NUMBER
      `the age in whole years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51 -- the weekly payment for loss of earning capacity of a non-earner` `the s 49 or s 50 amount` `the years likely not to be employed before pension age` `the pension age` `the age in whole years` MEANS
    IF `the pension age` MINUS `the age in whole years` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (max 0 (`the s 49 or s 50 amount` MINUS ((`the s 49 or s 50 amount` TIMES `the years likely not to be employed before pension age`) DIVIDED BY (`the pension age` MINUS `the age in whole years`))))

DECLARE `Kind of weekly payment` IS ONE OF
    `loss of earnings (s 44 or 45)`
    `loss of earning capacity (s 49, 50 or 51)`
    `the safety net income benefit (s 54A)`

DECLARE `Impairment for s 53(4), (5)` IS ONE OF
    `determined at 50% or more`
    `not determined 3 years after the accident, and likely to be 50% or more`
    `neither`

-- s 53 (lines 1560-1592): whether weekly payments are stopped on a day.
-- (1): not payable after the normal retiring age of the occupation or, if none, pension age; but an earner injured
-- after that age or "not more than 36 months before attaining that age" gets them "for a period not exceeding 36
-- months after the injury first manifests itself". READING: the 36 months run from the day of manifestation, and
-- "injured" is read as the day the injury first manifested. (1B): not payable while in prison (ss 44, 45, 49-51).
-- (2)(a): ss 49, 50, 51, 54A not payable after pecuniary loss damages are settled or awarded. (3): ss 49-51 not payable
-- after 3 years from manifestation (for a minor at manifestation, after attaining 21), and they cease when the total
-- paid under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54 "equals" the s 53(3)(b) limit; (4), (5): (3) does not apply where the
-- impairment is determined at 50% or more, or is not determined at 3 years and would likely be 50% or more.
-- Flat "not payable" / "not liable": TRUE (stopped) or FALSE (s 53 does not stop them).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of weekly payment`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day the injury first manifested itself` IS A DATE
      `the day the earner attains the age limit` IS A DATE
      `the earner was a minor when the injury manifested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the earner attains 21` IS A DATE
      `the earner is in prison on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded before the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total paid under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 53(3)(b) limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the impairment` IS AN `Impairment for s 53(4), (5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53 -- the weekly payments are stopped on the day` `the kind` `the day` `the day the injury first manifested itself` `the day the earner attains the age limit` `the earner was a minor when the injury manifested` `the day the earner attains 21` `the earner is in prison on the day` `pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded before the day` `the total paid under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54` `the s 53(3)(b) limit` `the impairment` IF
        `past the age limit`
    OR  (`the earner is in prison on the day` AND (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `the safety net income benefit (s 54A)`)))
    OR  (`pecuniary loss damages were settled or awarded before the day` AND (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `loss of earnings (s 44 or 45)`)))
    OR  (`the kind` EQUALS `loss of earning capacity (s 49, 50 or 51)` AND `s 53(3) applies` AND (`past the s 53(3)(a) day` OR `the s 53(3)(b) limit is reached`))
    WHERE
        `the 36 months` MEANS `months after` 36 `the day the injury first manifested itself`
        `injured within 36 months of the age limit` MEANS
            (`months after` (0 MINUS 36) `the day the earner attains the age limit`) `is on or before` `the day the injury first manifested itself`
        `the last day of the age limit` MEANS
            IF `injured within 36 months of the age limit`
            THEN `the 36 months`
            ELSE `the day the earner attains the age limit`
        `past the age limit` MEANS NOT (`the day` `is on or before` `the last day of the age limit`)
        `s 53(3) applies` MEANS `the impairment` EQUALS `neither`
        `past the s 53(3)(a) day` MEANS
            IF `the earner was a minor when the injury manifested`
            THEN NOT (`the day` `is on or before` `the day the earner attains 21`)
            ELSE NOT (`the day` `is on or before` (`years after` 3 `the day the injury first manifested itself`))
        `the s 53(3)(b) limit is reached` MEANS `the total paid under ss 44, 45, 49, 50, 51 and 54` AT LEAST `the s 53(3)(b) limit`

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- the safety net income benefit (s 54A)`

-- s 3(1) "severe injury", except in Part 6 (lines 212-214).
DECLARE `Severe injury head` IS ONE OF
    `a significant acquired brain injury`
    `paraplegia`
    `quadriplegia`
    `amputation of a limb`
    `burns to more than 50% of the body`
    `an injury specified by the regulations`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the head` IS A `Severe injury head`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- is a severe injury` `the head` IF NOT (`the head` EQUALS `none of these`)

DECLARE `Offer of suitable employment` IS ONE OF
    `no reasonable offer of suitable employment`
    `a reasonable offer received and not taken up`
    `a reasonable offer taken up, and that employment ended`

-- s 54A(1)-(4) (lines 1609-1621): a severe injury, a degree of impairment of 50% or more that would otherwise entitle
-- the person to payments under s 49, 50 or 51, and employment terminated (or self-employment no longer sustainable);
-- not if the person unreasonably refuses rehabilitation (2); it ceases on a reasonable offer of suitable employment
-- (3), unless the offer is taken up and that employment ends (4). The unreasonableness is a judgment: an input.
GIVEN `the head` IS A `Severe injury head`
      `the degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `the person would otherwise be entitled under s 49, 50 or 51` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment was terminated or self-employment can no longer be sustained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person unreasonably refuses a rehabilitation program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer` IS AN `Offer of suitable employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 54A -- the person is entitled to the safety net income benefit` `the head` `the degree of impairment` `the person would otherwise be entitled under s 49, 50 or 51` `the employment was terminated or self-employment can no longer be sustained` `the person unreasonably refuses a rehabilitation program` `the offer` IF
        `s 3(1) -- is a severe injury` `the head`
    AND `the degree of impairment` AT LEAST 50
    AND `the person would otherwise be entitled under s 49, 50 or 51`
    AND `the employment was terminated or self-employment can no longer be sustained`
    AND (NOT `the person unreasonably refuses a rehabilitation program`)
    AND (NOT (`the offer` EQUALS `a reasonable offer received and not taken up`))

-- s 54A(5) (lines 1622-1624): "must not exceed whichever is the lesser of (a) $965; or (b) ... 80 per centum of
-- whichever is the greater of the person's pre-termination weekly earnings or the person's pre-accident earnings".
-- The section states only the maximum (finding 6).
GIVEN `the s 54A(5)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-termination weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-accident weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 54A(5) -- the most the safety net weekly payment can be` `the s 54A(5)(a) amount` `pre-termination weekly earnings` `pre-accident weekly earnings` MEANS
    min `the s 54A(5)(a) amount` (0.8 TIMES (max `pre-termination weekly earnings` `pre-accident weekly earnings`))

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- the degree of impairment and the impairment benefit (ss 46A, 46C, 47)`

-- s 46C(2) (line 1345): "A number determined under the A.M.A. Guides must be rounded to the nearest whole percent",
-- with the example (line 1347, as converted) "95% must be rounded to 10% ... 84% must be rounded to 8%", read as 9·5%
-- to 10% and 8·4% to 8% (finding 2): a half rounds up.
GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46C -- rounded to the nearest whole percent` `the number` MEANS FLOOR (`the number` PLUS 0.5)

-- s 46A(3) (lines 1288-1293): binaural hearing loss converted to a degree of impairment: less than 10% NAL, zero; 10%
-- NAL, 10%; more, "the percentage equivalent of the number (rounded up to the next whole number) given by the formula
-- 10 + [0278 (NAL 10)]", read as 10 + 0·278 x (NAL - 10) (finding 2).
GIVEN `the binaural loss of hearing (per cent NAL)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46A(3) -- the degree of impairment for binaural hearing loss` `the binaural loss of hearing (per cent NAL)` MEANS
    IF `the binaural loss of hearing (per cent NAL)` LESS THAN 10
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the binaural loss of hearing (per cent NAL)` EQUALS 10
         THEN 10
         ELSE CEILING (10 PLUS (0.278 TIMES (`the binaural loss of hearing (per cent NAL)` MINUS 10)))

-- s 46A(1AA) (line 1223): "the Commission must not determine the degree of impairment within 3 months after the
-- accident": the first day it may is the day after the same date 3 months later.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 46A(1AA) -- the first day the degree of impairment may be determined` `the day of the accident` MEANS
    `days after` 1 (`months after` 3 `the day of the accident`)

-- s 46A(1A), (1B) (lines 1236-1251): with an accepted claim (other than one only for ss 57-59 or s 60(2A), (2C),
-- (2E)) the degree is "taken to have" been determined as 0% unless, within 6 years after the later of the accident and
-- manifestation (for a minor at the accident, 6 years from attaining 18), the Commission determines it, advises that
-- an impairment benefit appears likely, or receives a written application for an assessment.
GIVEN `the relevant day` IS A DATE
      `the person was a minor at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person attains 18` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 46A(1A), (1B) -- the last day of the 6 years` `the relevant day` `the person was a minor at the accident` `the day the person attains 18` MEANS
    IF `the person was a minor at the accident`
    THEN `years after` 6 `the day the person attains 18`
    ELSE `years after` 6 `the relevant day`

GIVEN `the relevant day` IS A DATE
      `the person was a minor at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person attains 18` IS A DATE
      `the person has an accepted claim of the kind s 46A(1A) needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the Commission determined, advised or received an application within the 6 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46A(1A) -- the degree of impairment is taken to be 0%` `the relevant day` `the person was a minor at the accident` `the day the person attains 18` `the person has an accepted claim of the kind s 46A(1A) needs` `the day` `the Commission determined, advised or received an application within the 6 years` IF
        `the person has an accepted claim of the kind s 46A(1A) needs`
    AND (NOT (`the day` `is on or before` (`s 46A(1A), (1B) -- the last day of the 6 years` `the relevant day` `the person was a minor at the accident` `the day the person attains 18`)))
    AND (NOT `the Commission determined, advised or received an application within the 6 years`)

-- s 47(1), (2) (lines 1352-1374): an impairment benefit for a degree of impairment "more than 10 per centum", from
-- the table, where "D" is the degree as a number. The table as printed ("$4 500 + ((D - 10) $1000)" and so on, the
-- multiplication sign lost in conversion: finding 2). s 61(2A) varies every amount in it each year.
-- Each band: the degree it starts from, its starting amount, its amount for each percentage point.
DECLARE `Impairment band` HAS
    `the band starts from`          IS A NUMBER
    `the starting amount`           IS A NUMBER
    `the amount for each point`     IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Impairment band`
`s 47(2) -- the printed band for` `D` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `D` LESS THAN 20 THEN JUST (`band` 10 4500 1000)
        IF `D` LESS THAN 50 THEN JUST (`band` 20 15000 1500)
        IF `D` LESS THAN 60 THEN JUST (`band` 50 60250 1750)
        IF `D` LESS THAN 80 THEN JUST (`band` 60 78000 2000)
        IF `D` LESS THAN 90 THEN JUST (`band` 80 120000 4000)
        IF `D` LESS THAN 100 THEN JUST (`band` 90 164000 8000)
        IF `D` EQUALS 100 THEN JUST (`band` 100 252000 0)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        GIVEN `s` IS A NUMBER, `a` IS A NUMBER, `p` IS A NUMBER
        `band` `s` `a` `p` MEANS `Impairment band` WITH `the band starts from` IS `s`, `the starting amount` IS `a`, `the amount for each point` IS `p`

-- The band a degree falls in, by the degree it starts from (for the varied amounts, given as inputs).
GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(2) -- the degree the band starts from` `D` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 47(2) -- the printed band for` `D`
    WHEN JUST `b` THEN JUST (`b`'s `the band starts from`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The benefit, for a whole-number degree after s 46C: nil for 10% or less; NOTHING over 100%.
GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER, `the starting amount` IS A NUMBER, `the amount for each point` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(2) -- the impairment benefit with the amounts` `D` `the starting amount` `the amount for each point` MEANS
    IF `D` AT MOST 10
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 47(2) -- the degree the band starts from` `D`
         WHEN JUST `the start` THEN JUST (`the starting amount` PLUS ((`D` MINUS `the start`) TIMES `the amount for each point`))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(2) -- the impairment benefit at the printed amounts` `D` MEANS
    IF `D` AT MOST 10
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 47(2) -- the printed band for` `D`
         WHEN JUST `b` THEN `s 47(2) -- the impairment benefit with the amounts` `D` (`b`'s `the starting amount`) (`b`'s `the amount for each point`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- death benefits (ss 57, 58, 59, 59A)`

-- s 57(2) (lines 1679-1688; formula F2, $103 210 x (125 - A) / 100): A is the age at death, 25 at least and 75 at most.
GIVEN `the age at death in whole years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(2) -- A` `the age at death in whole years` MEANS
    IF `the age at death in whole years` AT LEAST 75 THEN 75
    ELSE IF `the age at death in whole years` AT MOST 25 THEN 25
         ELSE `the age at death in whole years`

-- s 57(2)-(4) (lines 1675-1710; formulas F2-F5). The amount (the printed $103 210, varied) is replaced by
-- amount x B / (B + C) where there is more than one surviving partner (3); where dependent children would have had a
-- s 59 death benefit but for s 59(9) (4), they share amount / (S + 1) and the amount in (2) and (3) becomes
-- amount - amount / (S + 1), S being one or the number of surviving partners. Then less an impairment benefit received
-- under s 47 for the accident. READING: never less than nil. NOTHING where B + C is nil with more than one partner.
GIVEN `the s 57 amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the age at death in whole years` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the years this partner was a dependent partner` IS A NUMBER
      `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up` IS A NUMBER
      `there are children within s 57(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the impairment benefit received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57 -- the death benefit for a surviving partner` `the s 57 amount` `the age at death in whole years` `the number of surviving partners` `the years this partner was a dependent partner` `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up` `there are children within s 57(4)` `the impairment benefit received` MEANS
    IF `the number of surviving partners` GREATER THAN 1 AND (`B` PLUS `C`) AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (max 0 ((`the partners' amount` TIMES (125 MINUS (`s 57(2) -- A` `the age at death in whole years`)) DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS `the impairment benefit received`))
    WHERE
        `B` MEANS `the years this partner was a dependent partner`
        `C` MEANS `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up`
        `S` MEANS max 1 `the number of surviving partners`
        `the amount after s 57(4)(d)` MEANS
            IF `there are children within s 57(4)`
            THEN `the s 57 amount` MINUS (`the s 57 amount` DIVIDED BY (`S` PLUS 1))
            ELSE `the s 57 amount`
        `the partners' amount` MEANS
            IF `the number of surviving partners` GREATER THAN 1
            THEN (`the amount after s 57(4)(d)` TIMES `B`) DIVIDED BY (`B` PLUS `C`)
            ELSE `the amount after s 57(4)(d)`

-- s 57(4)(c) (lines 1702-1705; formula F4, $103 210 / (S + 1)): each child's equal share.
GIVEN `the s 57 amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of children within s 57(4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(4)(c) -- each child's share` `the s 57 amount` `the number of surviving partners` `the number of children within s 57(4)` MEANS
    IF `the number of children within s 57(4)` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`the s 57 amount` DIVIDED BY ((max 1 `the number of surviving partners`) PLUS 1)) DIVIDED BY `the number of children within s 57(4)`)

-- s 57(5)-(7) (lines 1712-1719): the Commission "is not liable to pay a death benefit under this section to a
-- surviving partner or dependent child" who (5) "receives an award or makes a settlement of damages in respect of the
-- death", or (6) is convicted of (a) murder or manslaughter involving the killing of the deceased partner or parent and
-- use of a motor vehicle, or (b) an offence under s 318(1) or 319(1) of the Crimes Act 1958 (or a corresponding law,
-- (7)) in respect of driving a motor vehicle that caused the death. Both bars reach the partner's s 57(2)/(3) benefit
-- and a child's s 57(4)(c) share. Only "is convicted": no "or found guilty".
GIVEN `the recipient received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is convicted of an offence in s 57(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 57(5), (6) -- the Commission is not liable to pay the s 57 death benefit` `the recipient received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death` `the recipient is convicted of an offence in s 57(6)` IF
        `the recipient received an award or made a settlement of damages for the death`
    OR  `the recipient is convicted of an offence in s 57(6)`

-- s 58(2)-(4), (6) (lines 1721-1767; formulas F6, F7): the greater of 80% of the earner's assessed earnings (A / 52,
-- A being what the earner could have earned in the 12 months after the death) and the dependent children amount; not
-- more than the lesser of the maximum and 100% of the assessed earnings; times B / (B + C) for more than one surviving
-- partner.
GIVEN `the figures` IS A `Weekly payment figures`
      `the earnings the earner could have had in the 12 months after the death` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of surviving partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the years this partner was a dependent partner` IS A NUMBER
      `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58 -- the weekly payment for a surviving partner` `the figures` `the earnings the earner could have had in the 12 months after the death` `the number of dependent children` `the number of surviving partners` `the years this partner was a dependent partner` `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up` MEANS
    IF `the number of surviving partners` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN IF (`B` PLUS `C`) AT MOST 0
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST ((`the single amount` TIMES `B`) DIVIDED BY (`B` PLUS `C`))
    ELSE JUST `the single amount`
    WHERE
        `B` MEANS `the years this partner was a dependent partner`
        `C` MEANS `the years each other surviving partner was a dependent partner, added up`
        `the assessed earnings` MEANS `the earnings the earner could have had in the 12 months after the death` DIVIDED BY 52
        `the single amount` MEANS
            min (max (0.8 TIMES `the assessed earnings`) (`the dependants' amount` `the figures` `the number of dependent children`))
                (min (`the figures`'s `the maximum`) `the assessed earnings`)

-- s 58(5) (lines 1750-1754): not payable "(a) after the expiration of five years after the death of the earner; or
-- (b) after the surviving partner attains the pension age -- whichever first occurs but if, at that time, the
-- surviving partner has a dependent child, weekly payments continue ... until the surviving partner ceases to have a
-- dependent child". READING: the last day of payments is then the day before the partner ceases to have one.
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day the partner attains pension age` IS A DATE
      `the partner will have a dependent child at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the partner ceases to have a dependent child` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 58(5) -- the last day of a surviving partner's weekly payments` `the day of the death` `the day the partner attains pension age` `the partner will have a dependent child at that time` `the day the partner ceases to have a dependent child` MEANS
    IF `the partner will have a dependent child at that time`
    THEN `the later of` `the earlier limit` (`days after` (0 MINUS 1) `the day the partner ceases to have a dependent child`)
    ELSE `the earlier limit`
    WHERE
        `the earlier limit` MEANS `the earlier of` (`years after` 5 `the day of the death`) `the day the partner attains pension age`

-- s 58(7)-(9) (lines 1769-1775): the Commission is not liable to make s 58 payments to a surviving partner (7) "in
-- respect of any period after an award or settlement of damages is made in respect of the death" (by anyone, unlike
-- s 57(5)), or (8) "in respect of any period" if the partner is convicted of the offences in s 57(6), the deceased
-- partner being the one killed (a corresponding law, (9)). READING: a weekly payment for a period after the award or
-- settlement is nil; a conviction makes every period nil.
GIVEN `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partner is convicted of an offence in s 58(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 58(7), (8) -- the Commission is not liable to pay s 58 weekly payments for the period` `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the period` `the partner is convicted of an offence in s 58(8)` IF
        `damages for the death were awarded or settled before the period`
    OR  `the partner is convicted of an offence in s 58(8)`

-- The child's other parent, for s 59(1)(b) (lines 1781-1784), as amended by No. 45/2026 s 18A.
DECLARE `The child's other parent` IS ONE OF
    `a dependent partner of the person who died, who supports the child`
    `a dependent partner of the person who died, who does not support the child`
    `a parent who is not a dependent partner of the person who died`
    `no other parent`

-- s 59(1), (8)-(10A): the s 59 payments for a dependent child of a person who dies. (1)(b): any of (i)-(iii).
-- (2): also a dependent child (s 58 meaning) of a surviving partner who later dies, not in a transport accident,
-- while entitled under s 58 (weekly payments and the education allowance only). (8): no weekly payment or education
-- allowance if a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58 and the child is that partner's dependant; (9): no death
-- benefit if a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58; (10): nothing after damages for the death are awarded or
-- settled; (10A): nothing if the child is convicted of the offences named.
DECLARE `Child's s 59 payment` IS ONE OF
    `the weekly payment (s 59(3))`
    `the death benefit (s 59(4))`
    `the education allowance (s 59(6))`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Child's s 59 payment`
      `the other parent` IS A `The child's other parent`
      `the surviving partner later died while entitled under s 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is a dependant of that surviving partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `damages for the death have been awarded or settled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is convicted of an offence in s 59(10A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 59 -- the payment is payable for the child` `the payment` `the other parent` `the surviving partner later died while entitled under s 58` `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` `the child is a dependant of that surviving partner` `damages for the death have been awarded or settled` `the child is convicted of an offence in s 59(10A)` IF
        (`the s 59(1) route` OR `the s 59(2) route`)
    AND (NOT `damages for the death have been awarded or settled`)
    AND (NOT `the child is convicted of an offence in s 59(10A)`)
    AND (NOT `barred by s 59(8) or (9)`)
    WHERE
        `the s 59(1) route` MEANS NOT (`the other parent` EQUALS `a dependent partner of the person who died, who supports the child`)
        `the s 59(2) route` MEANS
                `the surviving partner later died while entitled under s 58`
            AND (NOT (`the payment` EQUALS `the death benefit (s 59(4))`))
        `barred by s 59(8) or (9)` MEANS
            IF `the payment` EQUALS `the death benefit (s 59(4))`
            THEN `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58`
            ELSE `a surviving partner is paid under s 57 or 58` AND `the child is a dependant of that surviving partner`

-- s 59(3), (3A) (lines 1791-1797): "the sum of $59 for each dependent child, until the child attains the age of 18
-- years"; "on or after 1 November 2026" double that. READING: the doubling applies to the varied amount, and a child
-- is paid up to the day before attaining 18.
`the day s 59(3A) took effect` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026

GIVEN `the s 59(3)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `the day the child attains 18` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 59(3), (3A) -- the weekly payment for a child on the day` `the s 59(3)(a) amount` `the day` `the day the child attains 18` MEANS
    IF `the day the child attains 18` `is on or before` `the day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the day s 59(3A) took effect` `is on or before` `the day`
         THEN 2 TIMES `the s 59(3)(a) amount`
         ELSE `the s 59(3)(a) amount`

-- s 59(4)(a), (b) (lines 1799-1802): payable "if, at the time of the death, the child was under 18 years of age or, if
-- a full-time student, under 25 years of age"; "the sum of $103 210 divided by the number of dependent children".
GIVEN `the s 59(4) amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `the child's age at the death` IS A NUMBER
      `the child was a full-time student at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59(4) -- the death benefit for a child` `the s 59(4) amount` `the number of dependent children` `the child's age at the death` `the child was a full-time student at the death` MEANS
    IF `the number of dependent children` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `the child's age at the death` LESS THAN 18
            OR (`the child was a full-time student at the death` AND `the child's age at the death` LESS THAN 25)
         THEN JUST (`the s 59(4) amount` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`)
         ELSE JUST 0

-- s 59(6), s 59A (lines 1810-1814, 1855-1861): the education allowance, per annum, until the child attains 18, under
-- s 59 or, for a dependent child not entitled to it under s 59, under s 59A (inserted by No. 45/2026 s 18B).
GIVEN `the s 59(6)(a) amount` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `the day the child attains 18` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 59(6), 59A -- the education allowance a year for a child on the day` `the s 59(6)(a) amount` `the day` `the day the child attains 18` MEANS
    IF `the day the child attains 18` `is on or before` `the day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the s 59(6)(a) amount`

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- medical and like benefits (ss 60, 60A)`

-- s 60(1A) (lines 1867-1869): expenses are paid for "(a) if the application for compensation is made within 3 years
-- after the date of the transport accident, the period between the date of the accident and the date the application
-- is granted; or (b) in any other case, the period of 2 years immediately before the application is made". The first
-- day of the period. READING: the 2 years begin on the same date 2 years before the application.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 60(1A) -- the first day of the period for expenses` `the day of the accident` `the day the application is made` MEANS
    IF `the day the application is made` `is on or before` (`years after` 3 `the day of the accident`)
    THEN `the day of the accident`
    ELSE `years after` (0 MINUS 2) `the day the application is made`

DECLARE `Paid employment at the accident` IS ONE OF
    `full-time paid employment of 35 hours or more a week`
    `paid employment of less than 35 hours a week`
    `no paid employment`

-- s 60(2)(c), (2AB) (lines 1878-1885, 1900-1903): the most hours of child care a week, for a person who in the 30 days
-- before the accident was caring for a child unpaid (or was pregnant, or the domestic partner of a pregnant woman):
-- 10 hours (full-time 35 hours or more); x = 10 + (35 - hours) if less than 40, else 40 (less than 35 hours); 40
-- otherwise. Only during the first 5 years after the injury or death. (2AA): with home services under (d), 40 hours
-- combined.
GIVEN `the employment` IS A `Paid employment at the accident`
      `the hours a week of paid employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 60(2)(c) -- the most hours of child care a week` `the employment` `the hours a week of paid employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employment`
    WHEN `full-time paid employment of 35 hours or more a week` THEN 10
    WHEN `paid employment of less than 35 hours a week` THEN
        IF (10 PLUS (35 MINUS `the hours a week of paid employment`)) LESS THAN 40
        THEN 10 PLUS (35 MINUS `the hours a week of paid employment`)
        ELSE 40
    WHEN `no paid employment` THEN 40

-- s 60(2A)(b) (line 1913): "the reasonable costs incurred in Australia of a funeral, burial, cremation, monument ...
-- where the total amount of the expenses does not exceed $14 135". A "where" condition: when the total is over the
-- (varied) figure, the paragraph gives nothing (the ruling of 2026-11-05, periods (b)); fork line in NOTES.md
-- (finding 7: the other reading is a cap).
GIVEN `the funeral limit` IS A NUMBER, `the total reasonable funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 60(2A)(b) -- what is paid for funeral expenses` `the funeral limit` `the total reasonable funeral expenses` MEANS
    IF `the total reasonable funeral expenses` AT MOST `the funeral limit`
    THEN `the total reasonable funeral expenses`
    ELSE 0

-- s 60(2CA)-(2CD) (lines 1933-1939): a parent's lost wages visiting a dependent child in hospital: not the first 5
-- days (unless acute financial hardship, (2CD)); a day not more than one-fifth of the s 44(3)(a) amount; in all not
-- more than $10 000.
GIVEN `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 60(2CA) limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of lost wages` IS A NUMBER
      `the wages lost each day` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 60(2CA)-(2CD) -- the most paid for a parent's lost wages` `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the s 60(2CA) limit` `the days of lost wages` `the wages lost each day` `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship` MEANS
    min `the s 60(2CA) limit` (`the days paid` TIMES (min `the wages lost each day` (`the s 44(3)(a) maximum` DIVIDED BY 5)))
    WHERE
        `the days paid` MEANS
            IF `the Commission is satisfied of acute financial hardship`
            THEN `the days of lost wages`
            ELSE max 0 (`the days of lost wages` MINUS 5)

-- s 60A(1)(b) (line 2060): hospital services "received at least 3 years after the transport accident occurred".
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the day the hospital services were received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60A(1)(b) -- the hospital services were at least 3 years after the accident` `the day of the accident` `the day the hospital services were received` IF
    (`years after` 3 `the day of the accident`) `is on or before` `the day the hospital services were received`

-- s 60A(2)(a), (3), (4) (lines 2064-2068): a contribution for lost wages, a day not more than one-fifth of the
-- s 44(3)(a) amount; in all, under s 60A for one accident, not more than $3500.
GIVEN `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 60A(4) limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of lost wages` IS A NUMBER
      `the wages lost each day` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount already paid under s 60A for the accident` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 60A -- the most paid for lost wages after a later hospital stay` `the s 44(3)(a) maximum` `the s 60A(4) limit` `the days of lost wages` `the wages lost each day` `the amount already paid under s 60A for the accident` MEANS
    min (max 0 (`the s 60A(4) limit` MINUS `the amount already paid under s 60A for the accident`))
        (`the days of lost wages` TIMES (min `the wages lost each day` (`the s 44(3)(a) maximum` DIVIDED BY 5)))

§§ `Part 4 -- claims, decisions and reviews (ss 64-70, 77)`

-- s 68(1)-(3) (lines 2302-2317): a claim "within one year (c) after the accident or death; or (d) ... if no injury
-- manifested itself at the time of the transport accident, after any injury first manifests itself"; (3): a person
-- injured, or a dependent child of a person who dies, who was under 18 at the accident may claim "before attaining
-- the age of 21 years or within 3 years after the transport accident, whichever is the later". READING: "before
-- attaining 21" ends the day before the 21st birthday.
GIVEN `the day the time runs from` IS A DATE
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the claimant was under 18 at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claimant attains 21` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 68(1), (3) -- the last day to claim` `the day the time runs from` `the day of the accident` `the claimant was under 18 at the accident` `the day the claimant attains 21` MEANS
    IF `the claimant was under 18 at the accident`
    THEN `the later of` `the s 68(1) day`
            (`the later of` (`days after` (0 MINUS 1) `the day the claimant attains 21`) (`years after` 3 `the day of the accident`))
    ELSE `the s 68(1) day`
    WHERE
        `the s 68(1) day` MEANS `years after` 1 `the day the time runs from`

-- s 68(2): later, if the Commission "considers there are reasonable grounds for a delay", "before the expiration of
-- three years after the transport accident or death or after the injury first manifested itself". A judgment left to
-- the Commission: an input. READING: the last such day is the same date 3 years later; the minor's time in (3) is
-- "subject to subsection (2)" and is read as standing on its own.
GIVEN `the day the time runs from` IS A DATE
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the claimant was under 18 at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claimant attains 21` IS A DATE
      `the day the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68 -- the claim is made in time` `the day the time runs from` `the day of the accident` `the claimant was under 18 at the accident` `the day the claimant attains 21` `the day the claim is made` `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for the delay` IF
        `the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`s 68(1), (3) -- the last day to claim` `the day the time runs from` `the day of the accident` `the claimant was under 18 at the accident` `the day the claimant attains 21`)
    OR  (    `the Commission considers there are reasonable grounds for the delay`
         AND `the day the claim is made` `is on or before` (`years after` 3 `the day the time runs from`))

-- s 70(1), (3)(b) (lines 2332-2341): the Commission must, "within 21 days after receiving a claim", accept or reject
-- liability or make a reasonable request; if it does not, it "shall be deemed to have rejected the claim" and the
-- claimant may apply to the Tribunal "within 12 months after the end of the period".
GIVEN `the day the claim was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70(1) -- the last day for the Commission to respond to the claim` `the day the claim was received` MEANS
    `days after` 21 `the day the claim was received`

-- s 70(2): after a request, "within 14 days after receiving further information ... or within 21 days after receiving
-- the claim or making a request under subsection (1)(c), whichever last occurs".
GIVEN `the day the claim was received` IS A DATE
      `the day the further information or examination result was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70(2) -- the last day to decide after a request to the claimant` `the day the claim was received` `the day the further information or examination result was received` MEANS
    `the later of` (`days after` 14 `the day the further information or examination result was received`) (`days after` 21 `the day the claim was received`)

GIVEN `the last day for the Commission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70(3)(b) -- the last day to apply to the Tribunal after a deemed rejection` `the last day for the Commission` MEANS
    `months after` 12 `the last day for the Commission`

-- s 70(4) (line 2342): "If a person fails without reasonable cause to comply with a request ... within 28 days after
-- the request is made or such longer period as the Commission allows ... the claim lapses."
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70(4) -- the last day to comply with a request` `the day of the request` MEANS `days after` 28 `the day of the request`

-- s 77(1A), (2) (lines 2432-2436): by "the later of (a) 12 months after the person becomes aware of the decision; or
-- (b) if the decision has been the subject of an application for a pre-issue review under the Protocols, 3 months
-- after the Commission notifies the person ... of its decision on the application". NOTHING for a decision about an
-- interim benefit under s 47(3A), to which s 77(1) "does not apply" (fork line in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person became aware of the decision` IS A DATE
      `a pre-issue review was applied for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Commission notified its decision on the pre-issue review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 77(1A) -- the last day to apply to the Tribunal for review` `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit` `the day the person became aware of the decision` `a pre-issue review was applied for` `the day the Commission notified its decision on the pre-issue review` MEANS
    IF `the decision is about an interim impairment benefit`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a pre-issue review was applied for`
         THEN JUST (`the later of` (`months after` 12 `the day the person became aware of the decision`) (`months after` 3 `the day the Commission notified its decision on the pre-issue review`))
         ELSE JUST (`months after` 12 `the day the person became aware of the decision`)

-- s 64(1), (3), s 65(2), s 66(1)(a) (lines 2242-2278): the driver asked by a notice served by the Commission must
-- report "within 28 days of receiving the notice"; the penalty of $50 stops proceedings if paid "within 14 days after
-- the expiry of the period specified in the notice".
GIVEN `the day the notice was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 64(1) -- the last day to make the report` `the day the notice was received` MEANS `days after` 28 `the day the notice was received`

GIVEN `the day the notice was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 66(1)(a) -- the last day to pay the penalty` `the day the notice was received` MEANS
    `days after` 14 (`s 64(1) -- the last day to make the report` `the day the notice was received`)

-- s 45AC(4)(a) (line 1187): a seasonal earner's election "must be made in writing and be given to the Commission within
-- 14 days after the earner becomes entitled to receive any payment under section 44 or 45" (the Commission may waive
-- the 14 days, (5)).
GIVEN `the day the earner became entitled to a payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 45AC(4) -- the last day for a seasonal earner's election` `the day the earner became entitled to a payment` MEANS
    `days after` 14 `the day the earner became entitled to a payment`

-- s 49(4), s 50(4), s 51(5) (lines 1466, 1512, 1555): a statement of earnings "within two months after each
-- anniversary of the date on which the person first received a payment under this section".
GIVEN `the day of the first payment` IS A DATE, `the anniversary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 49(4) -- the last day for the statement of earnings` `the day of the first payment` `the anniversary` MEANS
    `months after` 2 (`years after` `the anniversary` `the day of the first payment`)

§§ `Part 6 Division 1 -- damages for death or serious injury (s 93)`

-- s 93(3) with s 47(6)(b) (lines 2583-2588, 1392-1395): the injury "is deemed to be a serious injury" if the degree
-- determined under s 46A, 47(7) or 47(7A) is 30% or more; but after two or more transport accidents with a total degree
-- of more than 10%, "section 93(3) does not apply unless the degree of impairment is determined to be 30 percent or more
-- as the result of one of the transport accidents".
GIVEN `the degree has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the degree determined` IS A NUMBER
      `there was more than one transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the highest degree from any one accident` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93(3) -- the injury is deemed a serious injury` `the degree has been determined` `the degree determined` `there was more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one accident` IF
        `the degree has been determined`
    AND `the degree determined` AT LEAST 30
    AND (    (NOT (`there was more than one transport accident` AND `the degree determined` GREATER THAN 10))
         OR  `the highest degree from any one accident` AT LEAST 30)

-- s 93(1), (2), (4), (6) (lines 2572-2601): damages only "in accordance with this section"; (2) a person may recover
-- damages if the degree has been determined and the injury is a serious injury; (4) with a degree under 30%, "may not
-- bring proceedings ... unless" the Commission is satisfied the injury is serious and issues a certificate, or a court
-- gives leave (a court may not, unless satisfied the injury is serious). The Commission's and the court's satisfaction
-- are inputs. NOTHING where, after more than one accident, the degree is 30% or more but no one accident gave 30%:
-- s 93(3) does not apply (s 47(6)(b)) and s 93(4) speaks only of a degree "less than 30 per centum" (finding 9).
-- FORK LINE: s 47(6)(b) measures the degree "as the result of one of the transport accidents"; read per accident,
-- s 93(4)(b) is met when each accident's degree is under 30%, and certificate or leave opens the way. A third reading:
-- with s 93(3) and (4) both out, s 93(2) governs alone and the person may sue if the injury is in fact serious. The
-- encoding keeps the literal total-degree reading and answers NOTHING.
GIVEN `the degree has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the degree determined` IS A NUMBER
      `there was more than one transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the highest degree from any one accident` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commission is satisfied the injury is serious and issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(2)-(6) -- the person may bring proceedings for damages for the injury` `the degree has been determined` `the degree determined` `there was more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one accident` `the Commission is satisfied the injury is serious and issued a certificate` `a court gave leave` MEANS
    IF NOT `the degree has been determined`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `s 93(3) -- the injury is deemed a serious injury` `the degree has been determined` `the degree determined` `there was more than one transport accident` `the highest degree from any one accident`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the degree determined` LESS THAN 30
              THEN JUST (`the Commission is satisfied the injury is serious and issued a certificate` OR `a court gave leave`)
              ELSE NOTHING

-- s 93(7), (11) (lines 2611-2617, 2631-2638): damages for pecuniary loss, or for pain and suffering, "only if" the
-- assessment before any reduction for the person's responsibility is "more than" the threshold "but less than" the
-- maximum (the assessment), or "more than" the maximum (the maximum), in each case "reduced first under subsection
-- (11) and secondly in respect of the person's responsibility for the injury". An assessment equal to the maximum
-- meets neither head and is answered as the text reads, nil (finding 8, fork line in NOTES.md). READING: never less
-- than nil. The responsibility is a share from 0 to 1.
GIVEN `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 93(11) reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 93(7) -- the damages that can be recovered` `the threshold` `the maximum` `the assessment` `the s 93(11) reduction` `the person's share of responsibility` MEANS
    IF `the assessment` GREATER THAN `the threshold` AND `the assessment` LESS THAN `the maximum`
    THEN `reduced` `the assessment`
    ELSE IF `the assessment` GREATER THAN `the maximum`
         THEN `reduced` `the maximum`
         ELSE 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
        `reduced` `x` MEANS
            (max 0 (`x` MINUS `the s 93(11) reduction`)) TIMES (1 MINUS `the person's share of responsibility`)

-- s 93(8), (9), (11A) (lines 2618-2619, 2640-2642): damages for a death under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958, not
-- more than $500 000, reduced by the compensation paid under ss 57, 58 and 59. READING: the maximum applies to the
-- damages after the reduction (fork line in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the s 93(9) maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `the damages assessed for the death` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation paid under ss 57, 58 and 59` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 93(8), (9), (11A) -- the damages for a death` `the s 93(9) maximum` `the damages assessed for the death` `the compensation paid under ss 57, 58 and 59` MEANS
    min `the s 93(9) maximum` (max 0 (`the damages assessed for the death` MINUS `the compensation paid under ss 57, 58 and 59`))

-- s 93(19) (line 2681): "the cause of action in respect of an injury arises on the day of the transport accident or on
-- the day on which the injury first manifests itself". READING: the accident day for an injury that manifested then,
-- otherwise the day it first manifested.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the day the injury first manifested itself` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 93(19) -- the day the cause of action arises` `the day of the accident` `the day the injury first manifested itself` MEANS
    `the day the time counts from` `the day of the accident` `the day the injury first manifested itself`

§§ `Regulative rules`

DECLARE `TAA party` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission`
    `the claimant`
    `the driver`
    `the person receiving weekly payments`
    `the injured person`

DECLARE `Response to a claim` IS ONE OF
    `accept liability`
    `reject liability`
    `request further information or a medical examination`
    `request information from another person`

DECLARE `TAA action` IS ONE OF
    `respond to the claim` HAS `the response` IS A `Response to a claim`
    `apply to the Tribunal for review of the deemed rejection`
    `give the further information or attend the medical examination`
    `make the report in the prescribed form`
    `pay the penalty of $50`
    `give the statement of earnings`
    `determine the degree of impairment`
    `advise that an impairment benefit appears likely`
    `apply in writing for an impairment assessment`

-- s 70(1), (3) as a rule. Clock: days from receiving the claim. Any response in (1) meets the duty; silence for 21
-- days deems the claim rejected, and the claimant may then apply to the Tribunal within the days given (12 months
-- after the 21st day, worked out by the date functions and passed in).
GIVEN `the days to apply to the Tribunal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAA party` `TAA action`
`s 70(1), (3) -- the Commission must respond to a claim within 21 days` `the days to apply to the Tribunal` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commission`
    MUST  `respond to the claim` `the response`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the claimant`
        MAY   `apply to the Tribunal for review of the deemed rejection`
        WITHIN `the days to apply to the Tribunal`

-- s 70(4) as a rule. Clock: days from the request.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAA party` `TAA action`
`s 70(4) -- the claimant must comply with a request within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `give the further information or attend the medical examination`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 70(4): the request was not complied with within 28 days (or a longer period the Commission allows) without reasonable cause, so the claim lapses; another claim may be made within the s 68 time (s 70(5))"

-- s 64(1), s 65(2), s 66 as a rule. Clock: days from receiving the Commission's notice.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAA party` `TAA action`
`s 64(1), s 66 -- the driver must report within 28 days, or pay the penalty within 14 days after` MEANS
    PARTY `the driver`
    MUST  `make the report in the prescribed form`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the driver`
        MUST  `pay the penalty of $50`
        WITHIN 14
        LEST  BREACH BY `the driver` BECAUSE "s 65(5), s 66(2): the report was not made within 28 days and the $50 penalty was not paid within 14 days after, so the driver may be prosecuted (1.5 penalty units), unless the Commission allows a later payment (s 66(1)(b)); s 64(4): no right to compensation is affected"

-- s 49(4), s 50(4), s 51(5) as a rule. Clock: days from the anniversary; the days to the end of the two months are
-- worked out by the date functions and passed in.
GIVEN `the days to give the statement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAA party` `TAA action`
`s 49(4) -- the statement of earnings within two months after each anniversary` `the days to give the statement` MEANS
    PARTY `the person receiving weekly payments`
    MUST  `give the statement of earnings`
    WITHIN `the days to give the statement`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person receiving weekly payments` BECAUSE "s 49(4), s 50(4), s 51(5): no statement of earnings within two months after the anniversary; at the next review no weekly payment is payable until it is given and the review is completed (s 55(3))"

-- s 46A(1A) as a rule. Clock: days from the start of the 6 years; the number of days is worked out by the date
-- functions and passed in. Any one of the three, within the period, keeps the degree from being taken to be 0%.
GIVEN `the days in the 6 years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAA party` `TAA action`
`s 46A(1A) -- within 6 years, an impairment determination, advice or written application` `the days in the 6 years` MEANS
        (PARTY `the Commission`
         DO    `determine the degree of impairment`
         WITHIN `the days in the 6 years`
         LEST  BREACH BECAUSE "s 46A(1A): no determination within 6 years, so the degree of impairment is taken to be 0%")
    ROR (PARTY `the Commission`
         DO    `advise that an impairment benefit appears likely`
         WITHIN `the days in the 6 years`
         LEST  BREACH BECAUSE "s 46A(1A): no advice within 6 years that an impairment benefit appears likely")
    ROR (PARTY `the injured person`
         DO    `apply in writing for an impairment assessment`
         WITHIN `the days in the 6 years`
         LEST  BREACH BECAUSE "s 46A(1A): no written application for an impairment assessment within 6 years")
